A hat server orphans forever when the process that owns it is killed. withHat is correctly bracketed (IntegrationSpec.hs:93/97/113) but finally cannot run under SIGKILL, so an OOM-killed or hard-killed test run leaves servers alive indefinitely -- 5 were found still running after 7 days, each burning ~0.5% of a core. Teardown should be structural, not dependent on graceful exit: PR_SET_PDEATHSIG on the spawned server, or a server-side exit when it has no clients and its owner is gone. | id:281235a8b20f915f932aec814bce4ff4108898f7
